    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CAPITOL STEREO\nTHE FULL SPECTRUM OF SOUND\nRECORDED IN LONDON\n'CAPITOL' OF THE WORLD\nCapitol\nRECORDS\nHIGH FIDELITY\nNorrie Paramor's\njet flight",
      "\" LONG PLAYING",
      "(LONG PLAYÍNG\nYOmX NOOWASNOH HITONOH",
      "CAPITOL STEREO THE FULL SPECTRUM OF SOUND\nRECORDED IN LONDON\n'CAPITOL' OF THE WORLD\nCapital\nECORDS\nHIGH FIDELITY\nNorrie Paramor's\njet flight",
      "\"CAPITOL' OF THE WORLD\nST 10190\nA SERIES OF OUTSTANDING INTERNATIONAL RECORDINGS\nCapitol\nSTEREO\nTHE FULL SPECTRU!\nOF SOUND\nside one\nengland\nHOLIDAY IN LONDON\nfrance\nRAINY NIGHT IN PARIS\nitaly\nVENETIAN BLUE\nspain\nBARCELONA\nsouth africa\nJUMPIN' JOHANNESBURG\nbrazil\nBRAZILIAN HANGOVER\nside two\nhawaii\nHONOLULU HONEYMOON\naustralia\nSYDNEY STOPOVER\nrapan\nEVENING ON TOKYO'S\nSUMIDA\nmexico\nSUNDAY AT CHAPULTEPEC\nspain\nMAJORCA\nitaly\nSUNSET ON THE TIBER\n-jetflight\nBrilliant Listening Music by England's Finest Orchestra\nNORRIE PARAMOR'S magic with popular\nmusic is well-known.\nHe has become, in three years,\nthe most popular and influential arranger-conductor\nin all of England.\nHis monaural hi-fi albums on Capitol\nhave met with success.\nAnd now Jet Flight is here - a remarkable stereo\nlistening experience in tune with the gigantic but\ngraceful Boeing 707 that effortlessly flies\nthe world's busy airlanes.\nParamor has added more violins, more 'cellos.\nmore violas, more woodwinds, and his colorful,\natmospheric arrangements reflect many of the globe's\nmost enchanting attractions in this newest of new\nalbums, gorgeously recorded\nin brilliant stereo sound in London.\nThis is not just another musical travelogue.\nFor Pianist Paramor, whose personal tastes run from\nDixieland jazz to Rachmaninoff concertos,\nhas abandoned the conventional concept of long-play\nrecording with Jet Flight.\nEach selection has its own instrumentation.\nSpecial effects were carefully -and perhaps\ndaringly —attempted by Paramor to make full use of\nmodern reproducing equipment. Odd instruments\nalso are heard. The \"highs\" are the highest,\nthe \"lows\" the lowest, and middle-range passages are\nround, full, complete- yet always\ndelightfully musical.\nThe long-awaited jet age is here, on\nrecords as well as in the sky.\nNorrie Paramor proves it with Jet Flight. Never\nhas there been a more genuinely entertaining record.\nPAN AMERICAN\n- Paramar nhoto hur Derek AlleY\nTUIC CTEDCA DECOON CHAIIIN DE DIAVEN ANIY WITH A CTEDEO CADTOINGE AND NEEDIE TAAVAIN DAMAGE"
    ],
